    <code code="11450-4" codeSystem="2.16.840.1.113883.6.1" displayName="Problem List"/>
    <title>Problems</title>
    <text><table><thead><tr><th>Problem</th><th>Clinical status</th><th>Verification</th><th>Code</th><th>Provenance</th></tr></thead><tbody>
  <tr ID="problem-1">
    <td>Fourteenth pregnancy at 37 (gravida 14, para 13), single live intrauterine pregnancy dated by ultrasound at 13 weeks 2 days; estimated due date July 12</td><td>active</td><td>confirmed</td>
    <td>O09.529</td><td>S — Synthetic modern prenatal care anchored to her documented fourteenth pregnancy; the dates are synthetic.</td>
  </tr>
  <tr ID="problem-2">
    <td>Grand multiparity: thirteen previous vaginal births, no cesarean or other uterine surgery; seven living children</td><td>active</td><td>confirmed</td>
    <td>O09.40</td><td>S — Synthetic modern problem anchored to her documented thirteen earlier births.</td>
  </tr>
  <tr ID="problem-3">
    <td>Short interpregnancy interval: conception about five and a half months after her last birth</td><td>active</td><td>confirmed</td>
    <td>O09.899</td><td>S — Synthetic modern problem anchored to the documented fourteen months between her last two births.</td>
  </tr>
  <tr ID="problem-4">
    <td>Iron deficiency anemia in pregnancy: hemoglobin 10.1 g/dL, MCV 76 fL, ferritin 9 ng/mL</td><td>active</td><td>confirmed</td>
    <td>O99.019</td><td>S — Synthetic finding; repeated pregnancies close together deplete iron. It echoes no documented diagnosis.</td>
  </tr></tbody></table></text>

